{"seconds": 624.567, "paras": [{"n": 1, "start": 0.54, "end": 9.33, "text": "For twenty years, Dexter Morgan has been television's favour", "cut": 9.81}, {"n": 2, "start": 10.29, "end": 18.38, "text": "And right now, he's back. Dexter: Resurrection, season two, ", "cut": 18.86}, {"n": 3, "start": 19.34, "end": 30.9, "text": "But there's a question the show never really asks. What if D", "cut": 31.48}, {"n": 4, "start": 32.06, "end": 41.36, "text": "Because in real life, one crime lab chemist got more than tw", "cut": 42.09}, {"n": 5, "start": 42.82, "end": 53.31, "text": "Welcome to the Fiction Files. I'm your Detective. Every stor", "cut": 53.74}, {"n": 6, "start": 54.17, "end": 65.21, "text": "This case has three questions. One. Would Dexter's science e", "cut": 65.74}, {"n": 7, "start": 66.27, "end": 80.46, "text": "First, the fiction. Dexter began as a novel, Jeff Lindsay's ", "cut": 80.89}, {"n": 8, "start": 81.32, "end": 92.5, "text": "Dexter is a blood spatter analyst for the Miami Metro Police", "cut": 92.93}, {"n": 9, "start": 93.36, "end": 98.81, "text": "And the whole show rests on one idea. The man the system tru", "cut": 99.59}, {"n": 10, "start": 100.37, "end": 101.93, "text": "Exhibit A. The gatekeeper.", "cut": 102.46}, {"n": 11, "start": 102.99, "end": 113.71, "text": "In a real trial, an expert can't just walk in and give an op", "cut": 114.14}, {"n": 12, "start": 114.57, "end": 124.95, "text": "The older one comes from a 1923 case about an early lie dete", "cut": 125.38}, {"n": 13, "start": 125.81, "end": 136.4, "text": "The newer one comes from a 1993 Supreme Court case called Da", "cut": 136.83}, {"n": 14, "start": 137.26, "end": 156.66, "text": "Now here's the twist. Dexter works in Florida. And Florida c", "cut": 157.09}, {"n": 15, "start": 157.52, "end": 168.56, "text": "Which means that for almost the whole original run of the sh", "cut": 169.09}, {"n": 16, "start": 169.62, "end": 176.31, "text": "So, Exhibit A. Dexter's testimony walks straight in. But get", "cut": 177.14}, {"n": 17, "start": 177.97, "end": 180.0, "text": "Exhibit B. The science on the stand.", "cut": 180.53}, {"n": 18, "start": 181.06, "end": 197.82, "text": "Blood spatter analysis is real. In 1971, a criminalist calle", "cut": 198.25}, {"n": 19, "start": 198.68, "end": 218.15, "text": "By the time Dexter came along, it was a regular part of real", "cut": 218.68}, {"n": 20, "start": 219.21, "end": 233.0, "text": "In 2021, a study funded by the US National Institute of Just", "cut": 233.48}, {"n": 21, "start": 233.96, "end": 238.08, "text": "One in nine. And when that goes wrong in a courtroom, it can", "cut": 238.66}, {"n": 22, "start": 239.24, "end": 257.74, "text": "In 1985, in the small town of Clifton, Texas, a teacher name", "cut": 258.17}, {"n": 23, "start": 258.6, "end": 280.64, "text": "Joe Bryan was convicted. More than thirty years later, Texas", "cut": 281.27}, {"n": 24, "start": 281.9, "end": 301.4, "text": "Now, to be fair to Dexter. He isn't a detective with a short", "cut": 301.83}, {"n": 25, "start": 302.26, "end": 311.589, "text": "So, Exhibit B. The science is real. But it's nowhere near as", "cut": 312.419}, {"n": 26, "start": 313.249, "end": 315.739, "text": "Exhibit C. When the analyst is the criminal.", "cut": 316.269}, {"n": 27, "start": 316.799, "end": 330.489, "text": "But Dexter's biggest problem in court isn't the science. It'", "cut": 330.919}, {"n": 28, "start": 331.349, "end": 344.329, "text": "In 2012, investigators found that a chemist named Annie Dook", "cut": 344.759}, {"n": 29, "start": 345.189, "end": 359.779, "text": "When it came out, every case she had ever touched was sudden", "cut": 360.309}, {"n": 30, "start": 360.839, "end": 372.659, "text": "Then it happened again. Sonja Farak, a chemist at another st", "cut": 373.089}, {"n": 31, "start": 373.519, "end": 389.219, "text": "And the courts made the rules very clear. Prosecutors must h", "cut": 389.649}, {"n": 32, "start": 390.079, "end": 406.769, "text": "So picture the real version. The day Dexter is exposed, it i", "cut": 407.299}, {"n": 33, "start": 407.829, "end": 413.539, "text": "And for the record, we found no scandal like this at Miami D", "cut": 414.069}, {"n": 34, "start": 414.599, "end": 419.459, "text": "So, Exhibit C. Dexter's evidence might survive a courtroom. ", "cut": 420.289}, {"n": 35, "start": 421.119, "end": 422.459, "text": "Exhibit D. The clock.", "cut": 422.989}, {"n": 36, "start": 423.519, "end": 435.419, "text": "So, how long would Dexter really last? Let's start with the ", "cut": 435.849}, {"n": 37, "start": 436.279, "end": 446.989, "text": "And Miami is one of the hardest places to get caught. In Mia", "cut": 447.419}, {"n": 38, "start": 447.849, "end": 461.819, "text": "So for one crime, the odds are close to a coin flip. But Dex", "cut": 462.349}, {"n": 39, "start": 462.879, "end": 473.849, "text": "Of course, real cases aren't coin flips. Killers slip throug", "cut": 474.279}, {"n": 40, "start": 474.709, "end": 483.629, "text": "But here's what real cases show. Long running killers are ra", "cut": 484.109}, {"n": 41, "start": 484.589, "end": 495.089, "text": "In April 2018, investigators caught the Golden State Killer,", "cut": 495.519}, {"n": 42, "start": 495.949, "end": 503.319, "text": "Gary Ridgway, the Green River Killer, was caught in 2001, wh", "cut": 503.749}, {"n": 43, "start": 504.179, "end": 510.849, "text": "Israel Keyes was a careful killer who travelled across the c", "cut": 511.279}, {"n": 44, "start": 511.709, "end": 520.769, "text": "And in Gary, Indiana, a computer program written by a journa", "cut": 521.199}, {"n": 45, "start": 521.629, "end": 539.699, "text": "Now picture Miami today. DNA from a crime scene can be check", "cut": 540.129}, {"n": 46, "start": 540.559, "end": 560.688, "text": "And what about real people who did what Dexter does, and wen", "cut": 561.218}, {"n": 47, "start": 561.748, "end": 575.668, "text": "So how long would Dexter survive? Not decades. In my judgeme", "cut": 576.498}, {"n": 48, "start": 577.328, "end": 578.348, "text": "Time for the verdict.", "cut": 578.978}, {"n": 49, "start": 579.608, "end": 592.288, "text": "On the science. Blood spatter analysis is real, it's still u", "cut": 593.018}, {"n": 50, "start": 593.748, "end": 603.688, "text": "On the double life. No real person has done what Dexter does", "cut": 604.518}, {"n": 51, "start": 605.348, "end": 611.718, "text": "Which gives Dexter an overall reality score of... three out ", "cut": 612.548}, {"n": 52, "start": 613.378, "end": 622.618, "text": "Dexter: Resurrection's season finale lands on New Year's Day", "cut": 624.567}], "words": [["for", 0.59, 1], ["twenty", 0.88, 1], ["years", 0.95, 1], ["dexter", 1.27, 1], ["morgan", 1.63, 1], ["has", 2.0, 1], ["been", 2.21, 1], ["television's", 2.71, 1], ["favourite", 2.95, 1], ["killer", 3.2, 1], ["by", 4.05, 1], ["day", 4.22, 1], ["he", 4.45, 1], ["reads", 4.62, 1], ["blood", 4.95, 1], ["for", 5.29, 1], ["the", 5.52, 1], ["miami", 5.75, 1], ["police", 6.08, 1], ["by", 6.95, 1], ["night", 7.1, 1], ["he", 7.41, 1], ["hunts", 7.56, 1], ["the", 7.86, 1], ["killers", 8.07, 1], ["the", 8.48, 1], ["system", 8.68, 1], ["let", 9.03, 1], ["go", 9.24, 1], ["and", 10.3, 2], ["right", 10.48, 2], ["now", 10.76, 2], ["he's", 10.95, 2], ["back", 11.18, 2], ["dexter", 11.86, 2], ["resurrection", 12.84, 2], ["season", 14.02, 2], ["two", 14.35, 2], ["is", 14.41, 2], ["out", 14.59, 2], ["every", 14.83, 2], ["friday", 15.19, 2], ["all", 15.61, 2], ["the", 15.86, 2], ["way", 16.34, 2], ["to", 16.54, 2], ["the", 16.72, 2], ["finale", 16.96, 2], ["on", 17.38, 2], ["new", 17.56, 2], ["year's", 17.81, 2], ["day", 18.23, 2], ["but", 19.41, 3], ["there's", 19.58, 3], ["a", 19.91, 3], ["question", 19.99, 3], ["the", 20.37, 3], ["show", 20.53, 3], ["never", 20.74, 3], ["really", 20.99, 3], ["asks", 21.28, 3], ["what", 21.91, 3], ["if", 22.17, 3], ["dexter's", 22.33, 3], ["job", 22.79, 3], ["was", 23.0, 3], ["r